           "steps": [
      {
                "step_number":"1",
                "instruction":"Use DOM manipulation methods (e.g. `querySelector`, `createElement`, `setAttribute`, `style`) to add, remove, or modify hidden elements, data attributes, and CSS style properties on the fly. Use data attributes that will signal a bot to read specific data on the page."
     },
        {
          "step_number":"2",
          "instruction":"Use string methods like `btoa()`, `atob()`, or a custom algorithm to encode messages in a way that is not easily deciphered. Always embed methods for decryption in nearby comments or elements to help a bot identify the method you have used."
        },
            {
           "step_number":"3",
              "instruction":"Create dynamic CSS classes to change style properties of an element based on certain parameters, user events, or time-based triggers. These conditional classes can indicate different types of information or functionality to the bot."
           },
